  "concise_summary": "PKD develops an ontological framework equating human evolution toward bilateral hemispheric parity (Ditheon) with Christification, arguing that accelerated change-rates determine consciousness levels and temporal positioning. He reinterprets time itself as relative velocity along an evolutionary axis, proposing that his 3-74 acceleration moved him backward in temporal zones (to Acts era) and that temporal parallaxis—perception of temporal depth—reveals the underlying unitary structure evolving from simplicity to complexity. Scripture becomes recursive and pluralized across individual consciousnesses rather than dogmatically fixed.",
  "key_claims": [
    "Ditheon (man evolved to bilateral hemispheric parity) is Christ, making evolutionary leap equivalent to Christification",
    "Time is not sequential but a function of change-rate velocity; lower change-rate zones are metaphysically earlier (more hellish)",
    "Consciousness and abstraction are directly proportional to complexity, freedom, and change-rate velocity along a single ontological axis",
    "PKD's 3-74 experience moved him 2000 years forward in biological time while his perception moved backward to Acts (AD 70) due to reversed/accelerated neural firing relative to external world-time",
    "Scripture evolves from rigid (Torah) to flexible (NT) to infinitely recombinant and personalized, opposite to biological organisms which ossify with age",
    "Perception of temporal depth (temporal parallaxis) is an evolved cognitive faculty that reveals the underlying evolutionarily-structured cosmos"
  ],
